Z||000022||Monkeyman||12-30-2000||10:54 PM||||I don't have any pics of my interior yet, but other than some small tears to the drivers side bolster, it's just about perfect.  It's been repainted (great job, WTIII <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">), too.  I'm in the middle of a serious stereo upgrade.  I have a Sony CDX-650 (something like that).  It has a black face so I plan on having a smoked Lexan face plate made so that it almost looks invisible when it's off.  I can control it with the door closed (no buttons on the door).  I'll get some of Mr. Mikes seat covers sometime in the next year or so.  The carpet is in great shape, too.  The radio/HVAC surround was glued but the glue is starting to wear out but I have another surround in good shape with the cut out for the aux gauges to replace it.||||reg||1
Z||000023||fotofrank||12-31-2000||04:31 PM||||I have had bad luck posting pics so here goes <BR>nothin'.<BR>My Car is an '84 SE 4cylinder automatic.<P>  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DASH.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DASH.jpg</A>    <p>[This message has been edited by fotofrank (edited 01-01-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000024||Tigger||12-31-2000||05:58 PM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/brentbefore5.gif">  <BR>Before<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/brentfinishstage6.gif">  <BR>After<P>The seats are grey and in great condition.  I put the tiger/zebra seat covers on to help keep from wearing them out.  Hehe, it's kinda funny, but ever since I put them on I've notice more people around here doing the same with their cars.  Probably just a coincidency.<P>Tina, mine's a Black Grant GT Signature Series 3 spoke wheel.  I like it, looks good.  They're not badly priced (I think around $50 at Pep Boys) and need a $10 adapter kit.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 12-31-2000).]||||reg||1
